{"id":"bang-tanker-1944-06-14","title":"A lone tanker, 14 June 1944","short":"A lone tanker · 14 June 1944","eyebrow":"Marianas lifeguard and Luzon Strait · BANG's second war patrol, in a pack with SEAHORSE and GROWLER","theater":"pacific","clock":"","window":{"from":"1944-06-13T17:00Z","to":"1944-06-14T13:00Z"},"gmt":true,"participants":[{"id":"bang","name":"BANG","of":"us","kind":"submarine","hull":"SS-385","co":"LCdr A. R. Gallaher","track":"ss-385-bang/2","sil":"balao","alias":"ss-385-bang","followed":true,"opposed":false,"colour":1},{"id":"tanker","name":"Tanker","of":"jp","kind":"tanker","sil":"tanker","note":"As BANG identified it (alone)","followed":false,"opposed":true}],"own":["us"],"against":null,"places":[{"name":"Luzon","lon":120.9,"lat":17.0,"inset":[121.3,15.5]},{"name":"South China Sea","lon":116.6,"lat":17.6},{"name":"Formosa","lon":121.0,"lat":23.6,"inset":[121.0,24.4]},{"name":"Iwo Jima","lon":141.32,"lat":24.6,"small":true,"inset":[141.3,25.4]}],"sections":[{"heading":"","paras":[{"text":"BANG's first attack of her second patrol, on a tanker alone, as typed on her attack sheet. No Japanese record of it has been found yet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Outcome","paras":[{"text":"BANG saw one hit forward of the stack, the tanker list and settle by the stern, and her crew put out boats; she claimed one 7,000–8,000-ton AO damaged. No Japanese record of the attack has been found. The Chichijima base force's June signal log has nothing for the 14th or 15th about a tanker torpedoed or her crew landed, only a Navy GHQ broadcast of a submarine \"certainly present\" at 1200 I at 22-30N 144-30E, four hours before BANG fired and some 80 nm east of her (p. 18) [[cite:jacar:C08030275500]]. The Navy's June summary has no entry for her either.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Reading the map","paras":[{"text":"Positions are BANG's own dead reckoning and star sights; lines between them are straight, and where she went in between is not recorded. Open circles are ships she sighted, at the target's position. As the clock passes each firing time a red ring pulses at BANG's position; hover a diamond for the attack sheet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Clocks","paras":[{"text":"BANG kept zone K (−10) for Attack 1 and zone I (−9) for Attacks 2 and 3, as her report does; GROWLER kept I on station, but SEAHORSE kept H (−8). Japanese records use Tokyo time (I, −9): the escort division's chart has HI-67's two oilers hit at 1515, seven minutes after BANG's sheet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"What is missing","paras":[{"text":"No Japanese record has been found yet for Attacks 1 and 3; those actions show only the American side. Where the Japanese record names only the ships that were hit, the rest of the convoy is described as the boats saw it.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Sources","paras":[{"text":"BANG's second war patrol report, NARA microfilm M1752 (74802784); SEAHORSE Patrol 5 (74845019); GROWLER Patrol 9 (74818866). The 1st Surface Escort Division war diary, June 1944, via JACAR (C08030141000, National Institute for Defense Studies). Sarawak Maru's record from combinedfleet.com, a secondary source, flagged where used. Coastline: Natural Earth.","aside":false}]}],"cites":{"jacar:C08030275500":{"href":"https://www.jacar.archives.go.jp/das/image/C08030275500","short":"JACAR","title":"Japan Center for Asian Historical Records (JACAR)","page":""}},"box":[142.067,21.617,144.85,23.55],"steps":[],"relief":[],"roads":"","fronts":[],"stations":{},"tracks":{"bang":[{"who":"bang","of":"us","utc":"1944-06-12T03:56Z","lat":22.9833,"lon":150.3167,"kind":"bt","ref":"BT","on_track":true,"local":"1944-06-12 0356 Z","raw":"22-59N 150-19E","note":"","fix":"","assumed":false,"cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p38","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0037.jpg","label":"p. 38","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"who":"bang","of":"us","utc"