5. ... Planed up to radar depth but there was no pip.","local":"1944-06-14 0903 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p03","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0002.jpg","label":"p. 3","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-13T23:19Z","state":"surfaced","depth":"","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Surfaced in a heavy downpour of rain.","local":"1944-06-14 0919 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p03","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0002.jpg","label":"p. 3","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-13T23:45Z","state":"submerged","depth":"","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Sighted target coming out of rain ... Submerged.","local":"1944-06-14 0945 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p03","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0002.jpg","label":"p. 3","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-13T23:46Z","state":"submerged","depth":"120 ft","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Went to 120 feet and for 25 minutes ran at full speed 8 knots heading for a 120° port track.","local":"1944-06-14 0946 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p03","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0002.jpg","label":"p. 3","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-14T00:18Z","state":"submerged","depth":"periscope depth","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Came to periscope depth and slowed.","local":"1944-06-14 1018 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p03","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0002.jpg","label":"p. 3","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-14T01:40Z","state":"surfaced","depth":"","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Surfaced and commenced end-around.","local":"1944-06-14 1140 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p03","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0002.jpg","label":"p. 3","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-14T05:49Z","state":"submerged","depth":"150 ft","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Submerged to 150 feet and for 45 minutes ran at standard speed 6 knots on course 070°T","local":"1944-06-14 1549 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p04","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0003.jpg","label":"p. 4","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-14T06:39Z","state":"submerged","depth":"periscope depth","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Came to periscope depth and slowed. ... With a nearly flat battery and no more time available decided to accept an unfavorable position","local":"1944-06-14 1639 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p04","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0003.jpg","label":"p. 4","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"utc":"1944-06-14T07:35Z","state":"surfaced","depth":"","charges":"","proximity":"","words":"Surfaced ran normal to direction of new station until target was out of sight","local":"1944-06-14 1735 K","cite":{"ref":"rg38-74802784/p04","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0003.jpg","label":"p. 4","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"}}]},"water":{"bang":{"seafloor":[{"utc":"1944-06-13T16:06Z"